Center of mass of combination of liquid and hollow portion (at position $\ell$ ), first goes down (to $\ell  + \Delta \ell$) and when total water is drained out, center of mass regain its original position (to $\ell$),  T = 2\pi \sqrt {\frac{\ell}{g}} 

$\therefore 'T'$ first increases and then decreases to original value.

